  "identifier": "datashield",
  "name": "DataSHIELD",
  "description": "Infrastructure and R package suite enabling non-disclosive federated analysis of sensitive research data across distributed sites. Analysts run statistical analyses simultaneously across multiple data nodes without raw patient data ever leaving each institution — individual-level data is never pooled or transmitted. Uses privacy-by-design principles with automated statistical disclosure control (output checking) to prevent re-identification. The dsBase package (server-side) runs over 12,000 validation tests per release. Built on OBiBa Opal and Molgenis as data node backends. Governed by an advisory board and steering committee based at the University of Liverpool; over a decade of production use with real-world consented data across EU and international research networks. GPL-3.0, R-based client/server architecture.",
